From: ahmedsaed <ahmedsaed2652003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: install cross binutils when building with clang

Downstream kernels such as linux-samsung-a51 build with clang but pass
-no-integrated-as, so they need the GNU cross assembler. init_compiler()
only installed "clang" for clang builds, so the kernel's cc-option checks
failed with "-fstack-protector-strong not supported by compiler".

Base: pmbootstrap ff954a63c7a5ead5045150f5a79f035259512df2
---
diff --git a/pmb/build/init.py b/pmb/build/init.py
index 5316e1e..d9d96f2 100644
--- a/pmb/build/init.py
+++ b/pmb/build/init.py
@@ -114,7 +114,8 @@ def init_compiler(context: Context, depends: list[str], cross: CrossCompile, arc
     elif "gcc6" in depends:
         cross_pkgs += ["gcc6-" + arch_str]
     elif "clang" in depends or "clang-dev" in depends:
-        cross_pkgs += ["clang"]
+        # Kernels built with -no-integrated-as need the cross binutils
+        cross_pkgs += ["clang", "binutils-" + arch_str]
     else:
         cross_pkgs += ["gcc-" + arch_str, "g++-" + arch_str]
     if cross == CrossCompile.CROSSDIRECT:
